<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable TextExpansion core (Phase 3 · Windows port · TextExpansion lane).

    This is the Windows peer of the macOS `&&`-trigger text-expansion engine:
      OpenBurnBarCore/.../TextExpansion/TextExpansion.swift            (model + matcher + planner + policy)
      OpenBurnBarCore/.../TextExpansion/TextExpansionKeyEventCharacters.swift (US-ANSI keycode map)
      OpenBurnBarCore/.../TextExpansion/TextExpansionInbox.swift        (keyboard composer)
      OpenBurnBarCore/.../TextExpansion/TextExpansionUsageStore.swift   (usage ledger + ranking)
      OpenBurnBarCore/.../TextExpansion/TextExpansionSnapshotStore.swift(JSON snapshot store)
      AgentLens/Services/TextExpansion/TextExpansionRuntimeController.swift (CGEvent-tap state machine)

    It targets plain net8.0 — NO Windows TFM, zero P/Invoke, zero UI framework, zero
    keystroke capture — on purpose: the SAME managed assembly the WinUI shell
    (net8.0-windows) links is unit-tested on the macOS authoring host today
    (`dotnet test`). This mirrors the already-proven OpenBurnBar.App.Settings /
    OpenBurnBar.Pretext portable-core pattern: a higher-runtime test project
    (net10.0) references this net8.0 library, and the WinUI app references it too.

    The REAL OS keystroke capture + injection (the CGEvent-tap peer: a Win32
    low-level keyboard hook + SendInput) is the OS adapter and is explicitly
    DEFERRED to bucket B/C. It plugs in behind the seams defined here:
      • ITextExpansionKeystrokeSink  — delete N chars + type the replacement
      • ITextExpansionSnippetSource  — supply the active snippet set
      • the injected clock (Func&lt;DateTimeOffset&gt;) — the suppress window
    Everything above those seams (trigger detection, the match algorithm, the
    runtime state machine, the snippet model, JSON snapshot store) is PORTABLE and
    carries real xUnit coverage in windows/tests/text-expansion/.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.App.TextExpansion</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.App.TextExpansion</AssemblyName>
    <!--
      Lets the net8.0 library be RESTORED/BUILT by the net10.0 SDK on macOS without
      a Windows targeting pack. It is a pure managed library, so no Windows facet
      is needed; this simply keeps tooling quiet on the authoring host.
    -->
    <EnableWindowsTargeting>true</EnableWindowsTargeting>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
